## Why This Is Asked
Assesss ability to design scalable, privacy-preserving streaming pipelines with per-tenant controls and lineage. It also tests cross-region delivery and data-exchange mechanics.

## Key Concepts
- Tenant-scoped masking and schema versioning
- Streaming ingestion: Pub/Sub + Dataflow
- Per-tenant partitioned analytics in BigQuery
- End-to-end lineage via Data Catalog; sharing via Data Exchange
- 24h per-tenant rollback using raw logs in Cloud Storage

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo Dataflow masking (simplified)
function maskPII(event) {
  event.email = hash(event.email).slice(0,8) + "@masked";
  // mask other PII fields
  return event;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test rollout and rollback for 24h per-tenant in production?
- How would you detect and handle schema drift across tenants/regions?

## Why This Is Asked
Probes multi-tenant data integrity, privacy, and governance at scale, including schema drift handling, masking, and lineage.

## Key Concepts
- Schema registry in Cloud Storage and Drift detection in Dataflow/Beam
- Row-level security with BigQuery policies for per-tenant isolation
- Per-tenant DLP masking and quarantine of invalid data
- Data Catalog lineage and end-to-end observability

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-Beam DoFn skeleton for schema validation
class ValidateSchema extends DoFn {
  processElement(context) {
    const record = context.element;
    // load canonical schema from GCS
    // validate fields, types, requireds
    if (valid(record)) {
      context.output(record);
    } else {
      context.output(NOT_VALID, record);
    }
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test schema drift in production without impacting traffic?
- How would you implement rollback across tenants if a schema change breaks downstream queries?
